WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.520
Previously, on Smallville.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.519
We'll always be there for each other.

00:00:04.519 --> 00:00:05.519
Forever.

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:08.519
I now pronounce you, husband and wife.

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:16.589
That thing that did this, what was it?

00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:19.589
Jarrell warned me about an ultimate destroyer.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:22.589
There was some sort of connection between us.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.589
I know that you feel it too.

00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:26.589
Okay, stop.

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:28.589
I'm gonna relieve Lois of her nurse's duties.

00:00:28.589 --> 00:00:31.589
And what I hear, he was lucky to make it past that creature alive.

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:33.590
You will eradicate the other cryptos.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:34.590
the other kryptonian.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.590
I am not going to hurt anyone.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.590
You have that free will.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.590
Say that Clark Kent, the unassuming journalist.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.590
Upside of the shadow into his red and blue,

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.590
creating two completely separate identities.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.590
I think there's a lot more to Clark Kent

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.590
that even Clark Kent doesn't want to admit.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.590
I'm going to fire me, Miss Mercer, go ahead.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.590
Clark, I don't want to fire you.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.590
In time, I'm sure the truth will be it itself.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:01:13.370
Bless me, Father, for I have sin

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:18.450
hurt many people, people that I care about.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.299
I'm here, my son.

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:23.299
Go on.

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:31.599
Something takes over without warning.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:43.459
Fighting ticket out.

00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:46.459
We all have our inner demons,

00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:49.459
but we must learn to control them.

00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:53.459
I'm trying, Father, the best way I know how.

00:01:53.459 --> 00:02:03.340
Rockless at night, searching for a way to save myself.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:13.400
Pips, thieves, there's so much those streets.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:27.569
One has lost their way.

00:02:27.569 --> 00:02:28.569
I reach out.

00:02:28.569 --> 00:03:03.009
Everything in my power, to put it to an end.

00:03:03.009 --> 00:03:09.680
Not the wickedness that I see.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.219
It keeps the beast from coming out.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:16.219
It makes me feel.

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:26.960
Stay on your righteous path, my son.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:34.960
Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:04:54.769
I haven't seen you this pump since you threw the touchdown pass that made the Crow's state champs.

00:04:54.769 --> 00:04:56.769
That is a tough one at top, Chloe, but last night I think I did.

00:04:56.769 --> 00:04:57.769
I think I did.

00:04:57.769 --> 00:04:58.769
I heard.

00:04:58.769 --> 00:05:00.769
It was quite the coming out party.

00:05:00.769 --> 00:05:05.769
Media outlets report that the red-blue blur made more saves last night than a Billy Graham

00:05:05.769 --> 00:05:06.769
Revival meeting.

00:05:06.769 --> 00:05:08.769
I thought you'd be happy.

00:05:08.769 --> 00:05:12.769
I mean, you're the one who convinced me to embrace my double identity and inspire the world.

00:05:12.769 --> 00:05:17.769
Yeah, but, Clark, did you have to make a guest appearance on every single traffic cam in town?

00:05:17.769 --> 00:05:21.769
slowing my super speed down enough to appear on video is not easy.

00:05:21.769 --> 00:05:23.769
I wasn't even sure it worked the first few times.

00:05:23.769 --> 00:05:26.750
Look, I'm all about your streak of primary colors making

00:05:26.769 --> 00:05:28.769
a splash, but this is more like a tsunami.

00:05:28.769 --> 00:05:31.769
If it means giving people hope, Chloe, I'll take that chance.

00:05:31.769 --> 00:05:37.769
I just want to make sure that your rush to inspire Joe Sixpack doesn't unmask Clark Kent.

00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:40.769
Chloe, working at the Daily Plan is a perfect cover.

00:05:40.769 --> 00:05:41.769
Right.

00:05:41.769 --> 00:05:42.769
So what?

00:05:42.769 --> 00:05:44.769
You're going to pull a quick costume change in the middle of the bullpen?

00:05:44.769 --> 00:05:45.769
I'm getting really good at it.

00:05:45.769 --> 00:05:46.769
Watch.

00:05:46.769 --> 00:06:02.740
Not to preempt your episode of America's Next Top Model, but you've got a little bit of a wardrobe malfunction.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:07.740
Clark, you're not exactly inspiring much confidence,

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.740
especially after what happened last night.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.740
After Lex died, all of his personal files were transferred into Luther Corp.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.740
What happens when Tess Mercer gets her hands on those?

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.740
You don't have to worry about Tess Mercer or me.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.740
All your attention should be on Jimmy.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.740
I saw him last night, Chloe. He's still pretty shaken up.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:29.029
I should have been able to protect him.

00:06:29.029 --> 00:06:31.029
Clark, you did everything you could.

00:06:31.029 --> 00:06:33.029
And thankfully now that Jimmy's been transferred to Met Jen,

00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:35.029
he's that much closer to home.

00:06:35.029 --> 00:06:52.310
I really think that the future looks a whole lot brighter for him.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.310
Jimmy, you know that that machine's already locked into a set dosage.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.310
It's not going to give you more, no matter how many times you hit the pump.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:05.040
You need to tell my doc that my pain is hummersized, not hybrid.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:15.819
Being in a hospital bed for five weeks really does a job on you.

00:07:15.819 --> 00:07:21.259
But, you know, maybe what you're going through isn't all physical.

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:23.259
Maybe you should talk to a psychologist.

00:07:23.259 --> 00:07:25.259
I don't need to shrink, Chloe, I need to go home.

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:32.129
Look, if you're doing fine, I will be too.

00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:33.129
I will be too.

00:07:33.129 --> 00:07:43.629
Jimmy, I wasn't the one that was practically mulled to death.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:47.389
That thing, it hasn't shown up again.

00:07:47.389 --> 00:07:52.569
The villagers already put away their pitchforks.

00:07:52.569 --> 00:07:54.569
I think he's gone forever.

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:57.980
You don't know that for sure.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:05.610
We would have heard about it.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.610
It's hard to believe that he just dropped in to destroy our wedding.

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:18.879
Just one of the pitfalls of getting hitched in the Meteor-free capital of the world.

00:08:18.879 --> 00:08:22.879
I guess it's just another sign that we were meant for each other.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:24.860
Because if the King Kong, a meteor-free

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:30.819
couldn't take you away from me. We're going to be together forever.

00:08:30.819 --> 00:09:53.100
Main medicine, please!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:10:52.769
I want you to drink, man.

00:10:52.769 --> 00:10:55.769
Nifty knapsack, Ken. Are you on your way to P.E.?

00:10:55.769 --> 00:10:57.769
I just got back from the gym.

00:10:57.769 --> 00:11:02.769
If you want to graduate from the bullpen to the corner office, you need to look the part.

00:11:02.769 --> 00:11:03.769
Well, thanks for the tip.

00:11:03.769 --> 00:11:06.769
I think we can find something a little less high school musical

00:11:06.769 --> 00:11:10.769
and a little more Louis Vuitton to carry around, whatever it is that you're hiding in here.

00:11:10.769 --> 00:11:15.769
Well, it really is just my gym stuff, and I don't think I want my boss going through my underwear.

00:11:15.769 --> 00:11:16.769
It's okay. I'll take you shopping.

00:11:16.769 --> 00:11:17.769
and we get back.

00:11:17.769 --> 00:11:18.769
You back?

00:11:18.769 --> 00:11:20.769
Where are we going?

00:11:20.769 --> 00:11:25.769
L.A. I'm announcing the new Mercer Media group at a press conference,

00:11:25.769 --> 00:11:28.769
and I need a friendly reporter to lob softballs.

00:11:28.769 --> 00:11:29.769
And you want me to go with you?

00:11:29.769 --> 00:11:31.769
Every cub reporter gets his big break.

00:11:31.769 --> 00:11:34.769
This just happens to be yours.

00:11:34.769 --> 00:11:36.769
Don't underestimate your talents, Kent.

00:11:36.769 --> 00:11:39.769
There's no telling where they'll take you.

00:11:39.769 --> 00:11:41.769
The sky is the limit.

00:11:41.769 --> 00:11:46.139
Do you have more important things to do?

00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:49.799
No, of course not.

00:11:49.799 --> 00:11:51.799
Good.

00:11:51.799 --> 00:11:53.799
Because the only reporters I want working for the planet

00:11:53.799 --> 00:11:55.799
are those who take their jobs seriously.

00:11:55.799 --> 00:12:16.970
Tony, hey!

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.970
You all right? I came right after the police called.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.970
Considering a man was murdered in this hospital last night, I'm doing pretty good.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.970
Look, I'm sorry I can't say the same thing for Davis Bloom.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.970
What happened to Davis? Was he hurt?

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:35.309
Hurt? No. No, Chloe, he was the killer. I saw murder someone right in front of me.

00:12:35.309 --> 00:12:43.100
What the hell are you doing here?

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:46.100
Well, thanks to you, I got cuffed.

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:50.100
thrown into a squad car last night, and then I spent the next six lovely hours getting grilled by a

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.100
homicide detective with the world's worst coffee bread.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.100
They let you out on bail?

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.100
Jimmy, they let me go.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.100
Since when does Metropolis PD let people get away with murder?

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.100
Look, I saw it.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.100
Jimmy, calm down.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:04.100
Yeah, you did see me. You did.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:08.100
But I didn't murder anyone. I was up here looking for a patient that I brought into the ER.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.100
It's a drunk driver, fatal accident. We called the cops.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:15.100
He ran. We had the entire night staff scattered around the hospital looking.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:21.500
And we didn't find him, but I found you wandering around the hall completely out of it.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.100
Look, I know what I saw, Chloe.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:28.600
Yeah, okay. Normally, your eyes could be trusted, but not last night.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.100
Your PCE pump, it was faulty.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.100
Gave you a double dose every time you hit the trigger.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:36.100
Now, if I had that much morphine in my system, I'd see some things, too.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:41.100
Davis, I was with Jimmy yesterday when he tried to give himself an extra dose, and the machine wouldn't allow it.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:44.610
Well, somehow it malfunctioned.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:47.659
Did you do anything to it?

00:13:47.659 --> 00:13:48.659
do anything to it?

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.850
Jimmy, hey, no one is going to blame me if you did.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:56.850
You were in a lot of pain.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.850
Nice, try, pal, but there was nothing wrong with that pump.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.850
Well, okay, ask the doctors.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.850
Or ask one of the nurses. They'll say the same thing.

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:09.850
I'm sorry, okay, I'm, uh, I'll get out of your way.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.850
Jimmy, I'm glad to see you're feeling better.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:31.679
I feel terrible.

00:14:31.679 --> 00:14:34.679
I know the tricks that pain killers can play on a person's head,

00:14:34.679 --> 00:14:36.679
and he sounds pretty heavy stuff.

00:14:36.679 --> 00:14:38.679
Still, you don't deserve to be cast as this.

00:14:38.679 --> 00:14:41.679
the madman and Jimmy's psycho thriller.

00:14:41.679 --> 00:14:45.679
The truth is, I'm not surprised he thinks of me that way.

00:14:45.679 --> 00:14:47.679
I did kiss his pride.

00:14:47.679 --> 00:14:52.559
Yeah, but he doesn't know that.

00:14:52.559 --> 00:14:57.980
Well, I, I just assumed...

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.980
I didn't, um, I didn't tell him.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.980
I didn't want to make a big deal out of it.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.980
No need to.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.980
Yeah, I was a way off base.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:14.679
Um, well, if I said anything or did anything

00:15:14.679 --> 00:15:15.679
to give him reason to hate me, I...

00:15:15.679 --> 00:15:18.679
to hate me, I hope we can get past it.

00:15:18.679 --> 00:15:22.679
I accept that he got the girl.

00:15:22.679 --> 00:15:25.679
And like I told you before, I'm moving on.

00:15:25.679 --> 00:15:29.120
I think that's a good idea.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:32.299
Oh, yeah.

00:15:32.299 --> 00:15:35.299
And if Jimmy needs anything, um, I'm here.

00:15:35.299 --> 00:15:48.690
When is it, you talk to me?

00:15:48.690 --> 00:16:03.019
Miss Cannot but wonder that if he had never met me,

00:16:03.019 --> 00:16:05.019
maybe this wouldn't have happened to him.

00:16:05.019 --> 00:16:57.330
It's nice of Oliver let you use his private jet.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.330
Luther Corp and Queen Industries are one big happy conglomerate now.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.330
We share all of our toys.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.329
Welcome aboard, Miss Mercer.

00:17:05.329 --> 00:17:07.329
We may have to reroute and land in Santa Barbara.

00:17:07.329 --> 00:17:10.329
Towers inform me there's a storm coming into LA.

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:12.329
Thank you, Captain Nichols.

00:17:12.329 --> 00:17:19.339
I want to understand you've been racking up a lot of frequent fire miles like me.

00:17:19.339 --> 00:17:23.339
No, there are a lot of foreign titans to charm when you're starting a global endeavor.

00:17:23.339 --> 00:17:28.339
Plus, I had to make a pit stop in Geneva to see a plastic surgeon.

00:17:28.339 --> 00:17:34.440
Oh, it wasn't a nit-tuck.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.440
Lex-Luther-Lograked me with symbiore.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.440
lojacked me with some biotech hardware,

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:39.440
and I had to have it sliced out.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.440
Lana told me what Lex put you through.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:46.579
I'm sorry.

00:17:46.579 --> 00:17:51.170
What about what Lex put you through?

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.539
He pretended to be your friend.

00:17:54.539 --> 00:17:56.539
For how many years?

00:17:56.539 --> 00:17:58.539
I'd like to think that there was a time

00:17:58.539 --> 00:18:00.539
when Lex and I had a real friendship.

00:18:00.539 --> 00:18:02.539
That wasn't a friendship.

00:18:02.539 --> 00:18:06.619
Clark, you were his obsession.

00:18:06.619 --> 00:18:12.140
Lex wanted so much to be like you.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:14.140
But he knew.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:16.140
He knew in his heart. He never could.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:22.819
Good likes to talk to you about me.

00:18:22.819 --> 00:18:26.119
He kept a journal.

00:18:26.119 --> 00:18:30.099
What is he?

00:18:30.099 --> 00:18:34.750
I was sworn to see Chrissy.

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:40.680
Are you thirsty?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.680
What?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.680
I am. I'm sure that Oliver keeps a bottle of the good stuff around here somewhere.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:20:46.670
He's stashed the body here too. You can get rid of it.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:52.839
The guy, the... the drunk driver is dead.

00:20:52.839 --> 00:21:29.210
It's right there, Davis.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:35.039
I don't know what you're seeing anymore.

00:21:35.039 --> 00:24:22.890
Oliver Queen would appreciate us finishing off his private reserve of 1990, Crystal.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.890
It's a long flight. I'm sure he wouldn't mind us drinking a few more glass.

00:24:24.890 --> 00:24:26.890
drinking a few more glasses.

00:24:26.890 --> 00:24:28.890
About Lex's Journal.

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:30.890
He's gone now, so you can tell me.

00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:32.890
Enough about Lex's Journal.

00:24:32.890 --> 00:24:35.890
Okay? I want to talk about you.

00:24:35.890 --> 00:24:41.029
We've had two bottles of champagne.

00:24:41.029 --> 00:24:43.029
You seem to have this inhuman ability

00:24:43.029 --> 00:24:45.029
to withstand the effects of alcohol.

00:24:45.029 --> 00:24:47.029
I have a strong metabolism.

00:24:47.029 --> 00:24:52.170
Me too.

00:24:52.170 --> 00:24:54.170
I can hold my liquor like no leather.

00:24:54.170 --> 00:24:57.170
It's in the Mercer gene.

00:24:57.170 --> 00:25:03.029
Daddy Dearest used to be able to finish off a

00:25:03.049 --> 00:25:06.049
before the lunch whistle blew at the mill.

00:25:06.049 --> 00:25:08.049
That sounds tough.

00:25:08.049 --> 00:25:13.349
Let's just say it wasn't the Norman Rockwell childhood

00:25:13.349 --> 00:25:15.349
that you had at the Kent Farm.

00:25:15.349 --> 00:25:18.349
Nobody's childhood is perfect.

00:25:18.349 --> 00:25:21.349
Yeah, but I bet you were red fairy tales at bedtime.

00:25:21.349 --> 00:25:28.470
I like what my dad did.

00:25:28.470 --> 00:25:29.470
I'm sorry.

00:25:29.470 --> 00:25:31.470
You don't, you don't need to hear that.

00:25:31.470 --> 00:25:34.170
It's okay.

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:41.509
I had these blue sheets

00:25:41.509 --> 00:25:44.509
that I used to pull up over my head.

00:25:44.509 --> 00:25:47.759
And it made me feel like I was underneath the ocean.

00:25:47.759 --> 00:25:55.759
ocean and I would hide in there and pretend to be the little mermaid waiting,

00:25:55.759 --> 00:25:59.759
dreaming of my prince to come rescue me.

00:25:59.759 --> 00:26:01.759
And then my dad would come in.

00:26:01.759 --> 00:26:09.779
The bastard shattered my eardrum.

00:26:09.779 --> 00:26:13.309
And he broke my arm.

00:26:13.309 --> 00:26:23.730
Three times.

00:26:23.730 --> 00:26:27.730
I bet you didn't expect the in-flight entertainment to include my true Hollywood story, huh?

00:26:27.730 --> 00:26:32.349
I'm just glad it has a happy ending.

00:26:32.349 --> 00:26:35.940
Look at you now.

00:26:35.940 --> 00:26:40.630
I think I'm just good at covering my tracks.

00:26:40.630 --> 00:26:45.000
I don't like you, Clark.

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:50.619
Why would I cover my tracks?

00:26:50.619 --> 00:26:52.619
I don't know.

00:26:52.619 --> 00:26:55.619
Why would Lex have an entire room devoted to you?

00:26:55.619 --> 00:27:01.849
I've seen the photographs.

00:27:01.849 --> 00:27:04.849
The crushed Porsche, the mushroomed bullets.

00:27:04.849 --> 00:27:07.849
I can't explain to you Lex Luther's delusion.

00:27:07.849 --> 00:27:10.849
Lex was a lot of things, but he was not delusional.

00:27:10.849 --> 00:27:16.730
We all have our deepest, darkest secrets.

00:27:16.730 --> 00:27:20.299
I just told you mine.

00:27:20.299 --> 00:27:38.640
There's nothing to tell.

00:27:38.640 --> 00:27:43.940
With me, it's what you see is what you can.

00:27:43.940 --> 00:27:58.259
How's the weather look in LA?

00:27:58.259 --> 00:28:00.259
These guys are all clear.

00:28:00.259 --> 00:31:17.299
What's happening?

00:31:17.299 --> 00:31:19.299
I got this cut in your ambulance when I saw the dead boy.

00:31:19.299 --> 00:31:27.799
Jimmy, get away from me.

00:31:27.799 --> 00:31:30.799
No. No, not until you tell Chloe what you did.

00:31:30.799 --> 00:31:32.799
She's on her way right now.

00:31:32.799 --> 00:31:35.799
You don't know what you're doing. You're not yourself.

00:31:35.799 --> 00:31:39.460
That's what you want everyone to believe.

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:47.859
See, I thought it was just a cover up.

00:31:47.859 --> 00:31:48.859
There's always you can ever offer yourself.

00:31:48.859 --> 00:32:17.069
Chloe, please, go. Get out of here.

00:33:10.450 --> 00:33:12.450
Well, there he is.

00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:13.450
The prince who came to my rescue.

00:33:13.450 --> 00:33:15.450
rescue.

00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:18.450
I would think parachuting out of a jet and landing in the Arizona desert

00:33:18.450 --> 00:33:22.450
would have slowed you down, but you seem to be doing just fine.

00:33:22.450 --> 00:33:29.450
I knew I was fine, the moment that I woke up in that Phoenix emergency room, to see you, standing by my side.

00:33:29.450 --> 00:33:35.519
Did you figure out what brought down Oliver's jet?

00:33:35.519 --> 00:33:37.519
Someone may have been trying to kill you.

00:33:37.519 --> 00:33:40.960
It is a dangerous world we live in.

00:33:40.960 --> 00:33:43.960
The NTSB is still investigating the explosion.

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:46.960
Have they found the pilot's body?

00:33:46.960 --> 00:33:47.960
No.

00:33:47.960 --> 00:33:48.960
I feel terrible.

00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:56.329
Why is it that he's dead and we're still alive?

00:33:56.329 --> 00:33:59.329
I guess I'm just lucky that you were in the right place at the right time.

00:33:59.329 --> 00:34:10.869
It's the lucky part was finding that parachute.

00:34:10.869 --> 00:34:12.869
Yeah, about the parachute.

00:34:12.869 --> 00:34:14.869
Where was that?

00:34:14.869 --> 00:34:16.869
I looked everywhere.

00:34:16.869 --> 00:34:18.869
You must have missed it.

00:34:18.869 --> 00:34:20.869
I found it stashed in the cabin locker.

00:34:20.869 --> 00:34:23.440
Just one?

00:34:23.440 --> 00:34:28.460
Yeah, I was able to strap it around both of us.

00:34:28.460 --> 00:34:33.250
Well, it was terrible as it all was.

00:34:33.250 --> 00:34:34.250
I hope that this experience.

00:34:34.250 --> 00:34:38.579
has brought us closer.

00:34:38.579 --> 00:34:45.059
I don't usually open up about myself to, well, to anyone, really.

00:34:45.059 --> 00:34:54.400
I understand that what you told me was a part of your past you'd like to keep private.

00:34:54.400 --> 00:35:03.550
If you were that I'm going to tell someone you seek it, I promise you I won't.

00:35:03.550 --> 00:35:06.550
Lex was right about you, Clark.

00:35:06.550 --> 00:35:08.550
There's not a bad bone in your body.

00:35:08.550 --> 00:35:14.119
My whole life I've had to deal with abusive people,

00:35:14.119 --> 00:35:16.119
people who took away my hope.

00:35:16.119 --> 00:35:19.559
But when I'm around you,

00:35:19.559 --> 00:35:23.559
Somehow, I feel safe.

00:35:23.559 --> 00:35:31.480
I'm just glad you're okay.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.480
I'd better get back to the planet.

00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:42.750
I wouldn't want you to think I'm not taking my job seriously.

00:35:42.750 --> 00:35:50.809
Clark, I may run his company.

00:35:50.809 --> 00:35:55.809
And I may live in his mansion, but I'm not Lex.

00:35:55.809 --> 00:35:59.059
You can trust me.

00:35:59.059 --> 00:36:19.230
You think she knows your secret?

00:36:19.230 --> 00:36:21.230
Well, she didn't exactly just come out and admit it.

00:36:21.230 --> 00:36:25.230
Well, does she have to? I mean, you saved her by flying out of a falling jet.

00:36:25.230 --> 00:36:26.230
First of all, we didn't fly.

00:36:26.230 --> 00:36:28.329
You sort of jumped, and she was unconscious the whole time.

00:36:28.630 --> 00:36:31.889
Well, whatever the case, she knows too much, and she's getting closer by the minute.

00:36:32.190 --> 00:36:33.730
So it's time to take extreme measures.

00:36:34.429 --> 00:36:37.690
You need to quit the Daily Planet and put the red-blue blur back into the closet.

00:36:37.989 --> 00:36:40.570
I'm not changing my life because Tess Mercer might know my secret.

00:36:41.949 --> 00:36:43.449
But she's beyond dangerous, Clark.

00:36:43.510 --> 00:36:44.570
She tried to kill Lana.

00:36:45.130 --> 00:36:47.030
Only because she was trying to destroy the power suit.

00:36:47.090 --> 00:36:48.369
She was desperate to stop Lex.

00:36:48.449 --> 00:36:49.929
I can't believe you're defending her.

00:36:51.530 --> 00:36:53.010
I'm not sure she's like Lex.

00:36:55.190 --> 00:36:57.590
Your ability to trust others.

00:36:57.610 --> 00:37:00.710
and always see the good in people is what makes you so special,

00:37:00.849 --> 00:37:02.690
but it's also what keeps getting you into trouble.

00:37:03.690 --> 00:37:08.860
You need to be careful, and I have to go.

00:37:10.559 --> 00:37:12.559
Jimmy's battle is finally over at MetGen,

00:37:12.639 --> 00:37:14.199
and I get to pick up my wounded soldier.

00:37:15.599 --> 00:37:17.119
I didn't know he was coming home today.

00:37:17.519 --> 00:37:17.980
How's he doing?

00:37:18.960 --> 00:37:19.360
Great.

00:37:21.579 --> 00:37:23.500
Jimmy and I made it out of the dark forest,

00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:27.380
and from now on, it's going to be one long, happily ever after.

00:37:28.280 --> 00:37:40.519
No more than three tablets a day.

00:37:41.239 --> 00:37:42.019
They can be highly addicted.

00:37:42.039 --> 00:37:44.039
Good luck.

00:37:44.039 --> 00:37:49.650
Hey.

00:37:49.650 --> 00:37:51.650
Are you not in this alone, you know?

00:37:51.650 --> 00:37:54.650
I know how much you enjoy playing Florence Nightingale.

00:37:54.650 --> 00:37:56.650
But I can take care of myself.

00:37:56.650 --> 00:38:07.829
Jimmy, I know you're upset, but trust me, I just stopped you from doing something you would have regretted the rest of your life.

00:38:07.829 --> 00:38:09.829
Davis came after me and I was protecting myself.

00:38:09.829 --> 00:38:12.829
But you don't believe me. You'd rather believe anyone else but me.

00:38:12.829 --> 00:38:15.829
People are watching us. Can we talk about this at home?

00:38:15.829 --> 00:38:20.230
We have no home, Chloe.

00:38:20.230 --> 00:38:25.250
Okay, you still have a lot of drugs in your system.

00:38:25.250 --> 00:38:26.250
No.

00:38:26.250 --> 00:38:28.250
No, no, no. My mind has never been so clear.

00:38:28.250 --> 00:38:32.250
I have put up with years of you taking someone else aside over mine.

00:38:32.250 --> 00:38:39.369
First Clark and then Davis?

00:38:39.369 --> 00:38:43.800
Trust me. You never have.

00:38:43.800 --> 00:38:49.360
Of course I trust you, Jimmy. I trust you with my heart. I'm your wife.

00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:52.360
And that's what I don't understand. Why the hell did you even marry me?

00:38:52.360 --> 00:38:55.360
Sir, settle down. I'm fine.

00:38:55.360 --> 00:38:57.360
We were just leaving.

00:38:57.360 --> 00:38:58.360
I'm not going anywhere with you.

00:38:58.360 --> 00:38:59.360
Come on, Jimmy.

00:38:59.360 --> 00:39:13.300
I was the biggest mistake of my life.

00:39:13.300 --> 00:39:40.670
Mr. Olson, Miss Mercer's not in.

00:39:40.670 --> 00:39:42.670
I cannot let you in here. I'm calling security.

00:39:42.670 --> 00:39:43.670
I'm calling security.

00:39:43.670 --> 00:39:44.670
Don't bother, I quit.

00:39:44.670 --> 00:39:48.670
And if you really wants to move more papers, tell her to put this at the top of her to-do list.

